.TH GXWID 8 2026-10-19 "Peios gxwi 0.0.7"
.SH NAME
gxwid \- manage GXWI network workers and desktop sessions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gxwid
.RB [ --unrestricted ]
.br
.B gxwid --print-capability-sid
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gxwid
owns the GXWI listener, machine certificate state, and session jobs.
It starts the restricted
.BR gxwi-server (8)
worker to parse network traffic and serve HTTPS.
It authenticates accounts through authd for Remote Interactive logons and asks peinit to start the configured compositor with the resulting token.
.PP
The listener survives network worker restarts.
Worker retries start at 1 second and increase to at most 30 seconds.
A worker that runs for at least 60 seconds resets the delay.
Session and overlay connections have a 10-second startup bound.
A timeout reconnecting to an existing session does not remove or restart it.
.PP
The browser-facing transport uses HTTP/1.1 over TLS.
Plain HTTP receives a redirect to HTTPS, without desktop content.
Internal session connections use HTTP/2 over local sockets.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --print-capability-sid
Print the network worker capability security identifier and exit successfully.
This takes precedence over normal service startup.
.TP
.B --unrestricted
Run the network worker without Peios token restriction, for development on a host without KACS.
Use environment listener and state-directory values instead of native registry and protected state setup.
Native authentication sessions are unavailable in this mode.
This does not qualify the service's native security behavior.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B Machine\eSoftware\eGXWI
controls the listener, compositor, shared machine overlay, and public sign-in labels.
See
.BR regman (1)
for each value's type, validation, default, and application time.
.PP
An overlay replaces browser access to ordinary sign-in and desktops.
It runs with the authority of its configured credential-free account.
A configured overlay that cannot start presents a not-ready page rather than normal sign-in.
.PP
Session locale values come from
.B Machine\eSystem\eLocale
and the authenticated user's
.B Users\e<SID>\eLocale
preferences, with a
.B C.UTF-8
fallback.
Existing sessions retain their environment when rejoined.
.SH SECURITY
Normal service execution uses SYSTEM authority and retains
.B SeImpersonatePrivilege
to transfer authenticated tokens to peinit through
.BR KACS_SCM_TOKEN .
The daemon does not mint principal tokens.
The network worker receives a restricted token and only the descriptors required for its work.
.PP
Write access to the compositor and overlay registry values determines which programs run with session or overlay authority.
Protect those values and the program files.
Verify an unfamiliar certificate's SHA-256 fingerprint through a trusted channel before entering credentials.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The capability identifier was printed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Required startup, configuration, key, or worker-management setup failed.
Normal service operation continues until a signal or process failure ends it.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GXWI_LISTEN
Listener address in unrestricted mode; the default is
.BR 127.0.0.1:7780 .
.TP
.B GXWI_STATE
Certificate directory in unrestricted mode; the default is
.B gxwi-state
relative to the working directory.
.TP
.B GXWI_SERVER
Path to the network worker; otherwise the daemon uses
.B gxwi-server
beside its own executable.
.TP
.B GXWI_RUN
Session socket directory; the default is
.BR /run/gxwi .
.TP
.B GXWI_RUNTIME
Per-user runtime root; the default is
.BR /run/gxwi-user .
.TP
.B GXWI_LOGON_SOCKET
Override for the authd logon socket.
.TP
.B GXWI_JOBS_SOCKET
Override for the peinit jobs socket; the default is
.BR /run/services/peinit/jobs.sock .
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /var/state/gxwi/key.pem
Private ECDSA P-256 key, readable by SYSTEM.
An unreadable existing key fails startup rather than being replaced.
.TP
.B /var/state/gxwi/certificate.pem
Public self-signed certificate.
Its names include the hostname at creation, localhost, and the loopback addresses.
.TP
.B /var/state/gxwi/certificate.sha256
Public SHA-256 fingerprint, written as colon-separated uppercase hexadecimal byte pairs.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Check the certificate and renew it if required, without restarting desktop sessions.
Checks also occur at startup and every 24 hours.
A generated certificate expires 365 days after creation and is backdated by 1 day.
Renewal begins with fewer than 30 days remaining, or when the validity interval violates the accepted policy.
.SH EVENTS
.B gxwid.certificate.renewed
records the preceding and replacement fingerprints and the replacement subject.
See
.BR evman (1)
for field definitions.
Existing TLS connections continue; subsequent connections receive the replacement certificate.
.SH NOTES
The first logon supplies the compositor's HOME, SHELL, PATH, GXWI_RUNTIME_DIR, and GXWI_DISPLAY_NAME values.
Rejoining a running session does not replace its environment.
.PP
The browser waiting page requires a working service worker under the browser's certificate and origin policy.
It caches its own assets, not an offline desktop.
Installation completing does not prove that a certificate was retained; verify the installed system independently.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gxwi-server (8),
.BR gxwi-hello (1),
.BR libgxwi (3),
.BR regman (1),
.BR evman (1)
